<section class="fragment-review-dimension" data-artifact="review-dimension" data-dimension="correctness" data-rev="1">
<style>
.fragment-review-dimension { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; color: #1a1a2e; }
.frd-filter-bar { display: flex; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 16px; }
.frd-chip { padding: 4px 10px; border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid #ccc; background: #f5f5f5; cursor: pointer; font-size: 13px; transition: background 0.15s; }
.frd-chip.active { background: #1a1a2e; color: #fff; border-color: #1a1a2e; }
.frd-chip[data-sev="high"] { border-color: #c0392b; color: #c0392b; }
.frd-chip[data-sev="high"].active { background: #c0392b; color: #fff; }
.frd-chip[data-sev="med"] { border-color: #e67e22; color: #e67e22; }
.frd-chip[data-sev="med"].active { background: #e67e22; color: #fff; }
.frd-chip[data-sev="low"] { border-color: #27ae60; color: #27ae60; }
.frd-chip[data-sev="low"].active { background: #27ae60; color: #fff; }
.frd-finding { border: 1px solid #e0e0e0; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 12px; overflow: hidden; }
.frd-finding-header { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; padding: 10px 14px; cursor: pointer; background: #fafafa; }
.frd-finding-header:hover { background: #f0f0f0; }
.frd-sev-badge { font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; padding: 2px 7px; border-radius: 4px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; }
.frd-sev-high { background: #fde8e8; color: #c0392b; }
.frd-sev-med  { background: #fef3e2; color: #e67e22; }
.frd-sev-low  { background: #e8f8f0; color: #27ae60; }
.frd-finding-id { font-weight: 700; font-size: 13px; }
.frd-finding-msg { font-size: 13px; color: #555; flex: 1; }
.frd-finding-status { font-size: 11px; color: #888; }
.frd-finding-body { padding: 12px 14px; border-top: 1px solid #e0e0e0; background: #fff; font-size: 13px; display: none; }
.frd-finding-body.open { display: block; }
.frd-finding-body code { background: #f4f4f4; padding: 1px 4px; border-radius: 3px; font-size: 12px; }
.frd-finding-body pre { background: #f4f4f4; padding: 10px; border-radius: 5px; overflow-x: auto; font-size: 12px; }
.frd-loc { font-size: 11px; color: #888; margin-top: 4px; }
.frd-fix { margin-top: 8px; padding: 8px; background: #e8f4ff; border-radius: 4px; border-left: 3px solid #2980b9; }
.frd-hidden { display: none !important; }
</style>

<div class="frd-filter-bar" role="toolbar" aria-label="Filter by severity">
  <button class="frd-chip active" data-filter="all">All (3)</button>
  <button class="frd-chip" data-sev="high" data-filter="high">HIGH (1)</button>
  <button class="frd-chip" data-sev="med"  data-filter="med">MED (1)</button>
  <button class="frd-chip" data-sev="low"  data-filter="low">LOW (1)</button>
</div>

<div class="frd-findings-list">

  <div class="frd-finding" data-sev="high">
    <div class="frd-finding-header" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-expanded="false">
      <span class="frd-sev-badge frd-sev-high">HIGH</span>
      <span class="frd-finding-id">CR-1</span>
      <span class="frd-finding-msg">Tag prefetch N+1 in syncLocalChanges chunk loop</span>
      <span class="frd-finding-status">open</span>
    </div>
    <div class="frd-finding-body">
      <div class="frd-loc">FirestoreSyncManager.kt:296-305 &middot; confidence: high &middot; surfaced: 2026-07-06</div>
      <p>The chunk loop calls <code>articleDao.getArticleTags(article.itemId)</code> once per article — O(chunk) serial DB reads. For a 200-article first-sync chunk this is 200 individual SELECT statements.</p>
      <div class="frd-fix"><strong>Fix:</strong> Add bulk DAO method <code>getTagsForArticles(itemIds: List&lt;String&gt;)</code> using <code>WHERE itemId IN (:itemIds)</code>, then replace the <code>associate</code> loop with <code>allTags.groupBy { it.itemId }</code>.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="frd-finding" data-sev="med">
    <div class="frd-finding-header" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-expanded="false">
      <span class="frd-sev-badge frd-sev-med">MED</span>
      <span class="frd-finding-id">CR-2</span>
      <span class="frd-finding-msg">performFullSync uses stale isFirstSync() (two-read path)</span>
      <span class="frd-finding-status">open</span>
    </div>
    <div class="frd-finding-body">
      <div class="frd-loc">FirestoreSyncManager.kt:414 &middot; confidence: high &middot; surfaced: 2026-07-06</div>
      <p><code>performFullSync()</code> still calls <code>firestoreBackupService.isFirstSync()</code> after <code>syncLocalChanges()</code> was updated to use <code>getUserMetaSnapshot()</code>. Results in two Firestore reads for first-sync detection on full-sync path.</p>
      <div class="frd-fix"><strong>Fix:</strong> Replace with <code>val meta = firestoreBackupService.getUserMetaSnapshot().getOrNull(); val isFirstSync = meta?.isFirstSync ?: false</code></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="frd-finding" data-sev="low">
    <div class="frd-finding-header" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-expanded="false">
      <span class="frd-sev-badge frd-sev-low">LOW</span>
      <span class="frd-finding-id">CR-3</span>
      <span class="frd-finding-msg">tagStates map precedence relies on second-pass overwrites</span>
      <span class="frd-finding-status">open &mdash; deferred</span>
    </div>
    <div class="frd-finding-body">
      <div class="frd-loc">ArticleListItem.kt:77-82 &middot; confidence: med &middot; surfaced: 2026-07-06</div>
      <p>Correct semantics today: <code>tags.forEach { false }</code> then <code>article.tags.forEach { true }</code> gives correct "article has this tag" state. Subtle for future maintainers. Not a bug; deferred.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>

<script>
(function() {
  var section = document.currentScript.closest('.fragment-review-dimension');
  if (!section) section = document.querySelector('.fragment-review-dimension');

  // Toggle expand/collapse
  section.querySelectorAll('.frd-finding-header').forEach(function(h) {
    function toggle() {
      var body = h.nextElementSibling;
      var open = body.classList.toggle('open');
      h.setAttribute('aria-expanded', open);
    }
    h.addEventListener('click', toggle);
    h.addEventListener('keydown', function(e) { if (e.key === 'Enter' || e.key === ' ') { e.preventDefault(); toggle(); } });
  });

  // Filter bar
  section.querySelectorAll('.frd-chip').forEach(function(btn) {
    btn.addEventListener('click', function() {
      section.querySelectorAll('.frd-chip').forEach(function(b) { b.classList.remove('active'); });
      btn.classList.add('active');
      var f = btn.dataset.filter;
      section.querySelectorAll('.frd-finding').forEach(function(card) {
        if (f === 'all' || card.dataset.sev === f) {
          card.classList.remove('frd-hidden');
        } else {
          card.classList.add('frd-hidden');
        }
      });
    });
  });

  document.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('sdlc:fragment-ready', {
    detail: { name: 'review-dimension', artifact: 'review-dimension', dimension: 'correctness', rev: 1, counts: { blocker: 0, high: 1, med: 1, low: 1, nit: 0 } }
  }));
})();
</script>
</section>
